# These files are HASHED in manifest.json, and the hashes are over LF bytes.
# Git's autocrlf would rewrite them to CRLF on checkout on Windows -- where the
# streaming rig actually is -- and every hash would then mismatch, so the kit
# would fail its own verify on the machine that runs the show. Checking them
# out byte-for-byte is not a preference here, it is what makes the manifest
# mean anything.
* -text
